-- title:
--   Crossing points of the special fibre are supersingular
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $M \ne 0$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. generated over $L$ by the image of the function field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible over $L$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`. Let $B =$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, with $X^{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} B$ and its open immersion `ιFin` into the two-chart model, whose structure map to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is `modelTo`. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field with $\varpi \mapsto 0$, and form the geometric special fibre, the pullback of `modelTo` along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, with first projection $\mathrm{pr}_1$. Assume $x$ is a point of this fibre with $\mathrm{pr}_1(x)$ in the open subset `chartFinOpen`, that $Z_1, Z_2$ are irreducible components of the fibre both containing $x$, and that $y_1 \ne y_2$ are points of $X^{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with `ιFin` $(y_i) = \mathrm{pr}_1(\eta_{Z_i})$ for the generic points $\eta_{Z_i}$, each $y_i$ being a minimal prime over the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $\varpi$. The conclusion is that there is a point $y$ of $X^{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with `ιFin` $(y) = \mathrm{pr}_1(x)$, with the image of $\varpi$ in the prime $y$, and such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon B \to \Omega$ whose kernel is $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet p Ω`: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $p$.
--
--   This is the crossing-point statement for the reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ in characteristic $p$: a point of the geometric special fibre lying on two components, detected by two distinct minimal primes over the uniformiser in the $j$-finite chart, is supersingular (Deligne–Rapoport, Katz–Mazur). It is used in the results on the intersection of the two components, on the triviality of the diamond automorphisms on the torus part, and on Hecke degeneracy maps over the special fibre.
